From: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: cq8725s-ayn-odin3: drop the absent redriver

The CQ8725S common dtsi routes the Type-C SuperSpeed lanes through an
NB7VPQ904M redriver at i2c5 0x1c. The AYN Odin 3 does not populate that
part. Every register of the chip reads back as an I/O error, while the
two aw88166 amplifiers sharing the same bus at 0x34 and 0x35 read their
real contents, so the bus is healthy and 0x1c simply does not answer:

  /sys/kernel/debug/regmap/4-001c/registers   00: XX    01: XX
  /sys/kernel/debug/regmap/4-0034/registers   00: 2066  01: 0311
  /sys/kernel/debug/regmap/4-0035/registers   00: 2066  01: 0311

This went unnoticed while pmic_glink_altmode still bound without a
mode-switch: the phantom retimer was described but never driven. Once
altmode started deferring until the switch registers, the connector came
up with that retimer as its mode- and orientation-switch, and every
Type-C attach began writing to a chip that is not there:

  gpi a00000.dma-controller: Error in Transaction
  geni_i2c a94000.i2c: DMA txn failed:3
  geni_i2c a94000.i2c: GPI transfer failed: -5

The burst runs for the whole attach and takes the audio DSPs down about
a second later - TZ sends a fatal notification to the cDSP and then the
aDSP, pmic_glink dies with them, subsystem recovery times out and the
board wedges hard on every dock.

Disable the redriver on this board and restore the direct connector to
combo-PHY path.

Signed-off-by: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-odin3.dts | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-odin3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-odin3.dts
@@ -350,3 +350,20 @@
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * No NB7VPQ904M on this board. The common dtsi routes the Type-C
+ * SuperSpeed lanes through a redriver at i2c5 0x1c which the Odin 3 does
+ * not populate, so keep the connector wired straight to the combo PHY.
+ */
+&typec_mux_redriver {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&pmic_glink_ss_in {
+	remote-endpoint = <&usb_dp_qmpphy_out>;
+};
+
+&usb_dp_qmpphy_out {
+	remote-endpoint = <&pmic_glink_ss_in>;
+};

-- 
